WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Connecting a media-generation engine — images, audio, video, even 3D — and generating something live, including a free local route.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.519
Settings, Media models, Add model.

3
00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:20.000
Four kinds: an OpenAI-compatible image endpoint, Stable Diffusion webui — free and local, but it needs the dash-dash-api flag — an OpenAI-compatible speech endpoint, and Replicate, which is the widest: image, audio, video, and 3D all through one connection.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.892
Turn on the Media tool group and ask for an image on camera.

5
00:00:22.892 --> 00:00:32.000
Two prompting habits worth showing: say what you don't want, not just what you want, and name the aspect ratio explicitly — or let the model write its own detailed prompt from a rough idea.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:39.541
For free local images with a GPU: run A1111 or Forge with the dash-dash-api flag, then point the Stable Diffusion webui model type at it.

7
00:00:39.541 --> 00:00:44.000
About six gigabytes of VRAM covers SDXL — no per-image cost, no external account.

8
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Speech works the same shape — an OpenAI-compatible speech endpoint, added the same way, generating audio from text on request.

9
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.611
The gotcha: video and 3D through Replicate are considerably slower and dearer than images — sometimes minutes, sometimes real cost per generation.

10
00:00:59.611 --> 00:01:05.000
Say so out loud before anyone leaves an agent generating video unattended, so nobody discovers the bill after the fact.

11
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.397
With models everywhere in this app, the natural next question is which one to actually use for a given job.

12
00:01:09.397 --> 00:01:11.000
Compare answers that in under a minute.

